Found while writing t/88_live_vllm_reasoning.t (karr #79).

lib/Langertha/Engine/vLLM.pm SYNOPSIS example 5 reads:

    $vllm->simple_chat(
        'Solve step by step: what is 7 factorial?',
        reasoning_effort => 'high',
    );

That does not do what it looks like. Role::Chat::simple_chat takes only
@messages and hands them to chat_messages, which turns every non-ref
argument into { role => user, content => $string }. The snippet therefore
sends THREE user messages: the prompt, the literal string
"reasoning_effort", and the literal string "high" - and no reasoning_effort
reaches the wire at all.

The two working forms are:
  - engine attribute: vLLM->new(..., reasoning_effort => "high") then simple_chat($prompt)
  - per-request control: await $vllm->chat_f(messages => [...], reasoning_effort => "high")
    (Role::Chat::_extract_controls picks the canonical control out of %opts)

Scope: fix the SYNOPSIS block. Only occurrence in the tree - grep for
simple_chat near reasoning_effort found nothing else.

